0007: early boot without Apple's crypto/trust-cache kexts on xnu-12377 (boot 27a: pc 0 from read_random).

- osfmk/prng/prng_random.c: 8796's 0014 HMAC-SHA256 DRBG, registered at EARLY_BOOT RANK_FIRST (boot 27a died at pc 0
  in read_random <- exe_boothash_salt: prng_funcs.generate was NULL). 12377 already hashes write_random with SHA-512.
- libkern/crypto/corecrypto_rand.c: with no g_crypto_funcs, kmem random contexts are SplitMix64 seeded by
  early_random() (rand.h: kmem generator need not be cryptographic, must not lock); cc_rand_generate -> read_random.
- bsd/kern/kern_trustcache.c (plain-XNU variant): load/legacy load return KERN_NOT_SUPPORTED, query/UUID check
  KERN_NOT_FOUND while the runtime is NULL (0001 keeps 0015's init guard; 12377 moved the entry points).
- SweetCPU: no processor_start() (12377: ml_processor_register boots the CPU; a driver's call is a no-op that
  returns KERN_FAILURE, which panicked).

